 "stimulus_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered full-width\">\n<thead>\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\"><strong>Dataset B Description</strong></td>\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\"><strong>Data</strong></td>\n\n</tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"left\">Weights of packages on a delivery truck (weights in pounds)\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"left\">Sample of 12 packages: 3.2, 9.1, 4.3, 1.9, 2.6, 4.7, 0.7, 1.3, 3.9, 6.4, 5.0, 25.4</td>\n\n</tr></tbody>\n\n</table>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 456649,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": " For Dataset B, calculate the mean and median (round answers to 1 decimal place). Use technology as appropriate. \n\n\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\mathrm{Mean} = 5.7,\\;\\mathrm{Median} = 4.1\"></span>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "To find the mean, add up the data values and divide by the number of data values, which is 12. The sum of the data values is 68.5, and dividing this by 12 results in the mean of 5.7.<br>\nTo find the median, order the data values from smallest to largest as follows:<br>\n0.7, 1.3, 1.9, 2.6, 3.2, 3.9, 4.3, 4.7, 5.0, 6.4, 9.1, 25.4<br><br>\nNext, locate the middle value in the ordered dataset. Since there is an even number of data values, add together the two middle values and divide by 2 to determine the median, which is 4.1.<br><br>\nTo find the mean using Excel, copy the dataset into cells A1 to A12. In any empty cell, type in: <br>\n=AVERAGE(A1:A12)<br><br>\nTo find the median using Excel, copy the dataset into cells A1 to A12. In any empty cell, type in: <br>\n=MEDIAN(A1:A12)<br><br>\nTo find the mean and median using Python, follow this outline:\n<pre class=\"python\" lang=\"python\"># import the statistics library import statistics\n# define a dataset of 12 numbers\nweights = [3.2, 9.1, 4.3, 1.9, 2.6, 4.7, 0.7, 1.3, 3.9, 6.4, 5.0, 25.4]\n# execute the statistics.mean() function on this list\nprint(statistics.mean(weights))\n# execute the statistics.median() function on this list \nprint(statistics.median(weights))\n</pre>\n \n\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
